-- 008 — the tarmac map lands, and the first position definitions with it.
--
-- Two of the deliverables Rodeo Express owed (spec 11.3, 11.4) arrived in
-- August 2026: a description of the ground detailed enough to draw, and the
-- 2026 Committee Handbook to scrape position write-ups from.
--
-- map_ref: every one of the 98 positions gets the id of its marker in
-- public/assets/map/tarmac.svg. Both sides are generated by
-- bin/gen-tarmac-map.php from one naming rule, and its --check mode holds
-- this file and the SVG to the generator. When the committee corrects a
-- placement, the marker moves in the SVG; the ids — and these rows — do not
-- change.
--
-- definition: the "What's this?" text (spec 6.5), written per family as
-- 11.3 asks. Only what the handbook and the committee's description actually
-- support is written; the rest stays NULL and the UI keeps saying the
-- write-up is still owed, which is the truth. Nothing here is invented.
--
-- Pure data, so it opts into a transaction:
-- resm:atomic

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- map_ref, one row per position (generated: bin/gen-tarmac-map.php --refs)
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

